@host = http://localhost:5161
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "P@$$w0rd"
}

### Login (run this first, the token is saved automatically)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "P@$$w0rd"
}

### Who am I (checks the token)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Municipalities (public - used by the iOS city picker)
GET {{host}}/api/municipalities

### A2: election summary for one municipality
GET {{host}}/api/elections?city=Burnaby
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2: positions / offices for one municipality
GET {{host}}/api/positions?city=Pitt Meadows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/offices?city=Burnaby
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2: candidates for one municipality
GET {{host}}/api/candidates?city=Burnaby
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2: candidate 1 is in Pitt Meadows, so asking for it in Burnaby -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/candidates/1?city=Burnaby
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/candidates/search?city=Burnaby&name=park
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2: no city -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/candidates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2: no token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/candidates?city=Burnaby
